      "side": 1,
      "message": "Now that I see the test for filegroup, I think there\u0027s a use case that requires some more thinking on this line.\n\nSay we have these Soong modules\n\n```\nfilegroup {\n    name: \"a_aidl_filegroup\",\n    srcs: [\"a/**/*.aidl\"],\n    path: \"a\",   \n}\nfilegroup {\n    name: \"b_aidl_filegroup\",\n    srcs: [\"b/**/*.aidl\"],\n    path: \"b\",   \n}\njava_library {\n    name: \"foo\",\n    srcs: [\":a_aidl_filegroup\", \":b_aidl_filegroup\"] \n}\n```\n\nIn Bazel, they will be converted to\n\n```\nfilegroup(\n    name \u003d \"a_aidl_filegroup\",\n    srcs \u003d [\"a/**/*.aidl\"],\n}\nfilegroup(\n    name \u003d \"b_aidl_filegroup\",\n    srcs \u003d [\"b/**/*.aidl\"],\n)\n\naidl_library(\n    name \u003d \"foo_aidl_library\",\n    srcs \u003d [\":a_aidl_filegroup\", \":b_aidl_filegroup\"]\n)\njava_aidl_library(\n    name \u003d \"foo_java_aidl_library\",\n    deps \u003d [\":foo_aidl_library\"]\n)\n\njava_library(\n    name \u003d \"foo\",\n    deps \u003d \":foo_java_aidl_library\"]\n)\n```\n\nI believe this won\u0027t work because the basepath is different in each filegroup of aidl files. The `strip_import_prefix` attribute proposed in the design doc isn\u0027t feasible because we have two prefixes to strip.\n\n\nInstead, I think we should create an `aidl_library` target for each filegroup.\n\n```\nfilegroup(\n    name \u003d \"a_aidl_filegroup\",\n    srcs \u003d [\"a/**/*.aidl\"],\n}\nfilegroup(\n    name \u003d \"b_aidl_filegroup\",\n    srcs \u003d [\"b/**/*.aidl\"],\n)\n\naidl_library(\n    name \u003d \"foo_a_aidl_library\",\n    srcs \u003d [\":a_aidl_filegroup\"],\n    (later) strip_import_prefix \u003d \"a\"\n)\naidl_library(\n    name \u003d \"foo_b_aidl_library\",\n    srcs \u003d \":b_aidl_filegroup\"]\n    (later) strip_import_prefix \u003d \"b\"\n)\njava_aidl_library(\n    name \u003d \"foo_java_aidl_library\",\n    deps \u003d [\":foo_a_aidl_library\", \":foo_b_aidl_library\"]\n)\n\njava_library(\n    name \u003d \"foo\",\n    deps \u003d \":foo_java_aidl_library\"]\n)\n```\n\nWith this approach, we will have a solution to handle the `path` prop in filegroup.",
